<title>USA: Raines says no &quot;meat-axe&quot; approach to programs.</title>
<headline>Raines says no &quot;meat-axe&quot; approach to programs.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>White House Budget Director Franklin Raines said Friday the administration would not take an indiscriminate approach to cutting federal programs in its effort to balance the budget.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not going to be taking a meat-axe approach and saying everybody is going to be cut,&quot; he told a National Contract Management Association luncheon.</p>
<p>&quot;We're going to be looking program by program,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
